# =============================================================================
# OASSE AI Infra Hackathon - root .gitignore
#
# Ignores local state, secrets, caches, and generated output only.
# Source, documentation, tests, test fixtures, example configuration, and
# everything judges need to clone and run the demo stay tracked.
#
# Convention: directory names that could plausibly also name a source, docs,
# or tests directory (data, models, output, receipts, env, camera, ...) are
# anchored to the repository root and the application root so they can never
# swallow tracked code. Generated output is expected at one of those two
# roots. Unambiguous names (tool caches, dot-directories, secrets) match at
# any depth. Example configuration (*.example.*) is always tracked.
# =============================================================================

# --- Environment files (templates stay tracked) ------------------------------
.env
.env.*
.envrc
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
!*.env.example

# --- Python bytecode and caches ----------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python

# --- Virtual environments ----------------------------------------------------
.venv/
.direnv/
pyvenv.cfg
/venv/
/env/
/ENV/
/oasse-ai-infra-hackathon/venv/
/oasse-ai-infra-hackathon/env/
/oasse-ai-infra-hackathon/ENV/

